<title>UK: Severn Trent H1 pretax, pre-exceps up 6.6pct.</title>
<headline>Severn Trent H1 pretax, pre-exceps up 6.6pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		47.4		   vs 45.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 10.5		   vs 9.2</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-exceps     201.5		  vs 189</p>
<p> Pretax		     197		    vs 189</p>
<p> Turnover		   597		    vs 568.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 193 to 210 million stg. Severn Trent Water Plc said it took exceptional costs of 4.5 million stg after its aborted bid for South West Water.Earnings per share are before exceptionals.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 217.6		  vs 211.9</p>
<p> Interest		   22.4 payable	 vs 24.7 payable</p>
<p> Tax			  27.2		   vs 23.7</p>
<p> Net taxed		  169.8		  vs 165.3</p>
<p> Retained profit	  130.9		  vs 131.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   April 7, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  January 8, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 30, 1996</p>
<p>Note - Severn Trent said it intended to reduce dividend cover to around two times earnings by the year 2000.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
